    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26792" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Līrīnus</span></b> , i
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lērīna</span></b> ,
		ae), f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ληρίνη</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an island on the coast
				of</i> Gallia Narbonensis, <i>opposite to</i>
			Antipolis (the modern Antibes), now <i>St. Honorat</i>
			(one of the islands <i>De Le´rins</i>),
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				3, 5, 11, § 79</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sid.
				Carm. 16, 104</span></i>. —Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Līrīnensis</span></b> ,
				<i>adj., Lirinian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cenobium Lirinense,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 8, 14</span></i>
			.</div>
